sn35.235:5.3 starts: it is possible that one will go to one of two destinations:
sn35.238:5.5 starts: ‘There is this great expanse of water whose near shore is dangerous
sn35.245:7.2 starts: ‘Sir, what is a kiṁsuka tree like?’ The other might answer:
sn35.30:1.16 starts: mind-consciousness … mind-contact … and as to
sn35.30:1.17 starts: mind-contact … and as to whatever feeling arises
sn35.30:1.18 starts: and as to whatever feeling arises with mind-contact as condition
sn35.53:2.2 starts: When one knows and sees forms as impermanent …
sn35.88:18.6 starts: and he himself, during that same rains, realized the three true knowledges.
sn35.92:2.4 starts: and, further, he would meet with vexation.
